 ### 2240 — Apple UI fixture infrastructure uses split build-host/runtime evidence (TASK-260715-1idq8c)
 - IMPLEMENTATION: One Swift package target owns BEM-like identifiers, typed launch keys, fail-closed non-networked configuration, and 18 deterministic profile/trust/capability/failure/diagnostic/onboarding/migration/privacy fixtures. Two isolated fixture hosts and two shared-source UI-test targets provide Page Objects, condition waits, step screenshots, xcresult extraction, and controlled snapshot diff packets without importing NetworkExtension or either production adapter.
 - VERIFICATION: The iPhone 17 Pro iOS 26.5 Simulator smoke passed unsigned, emitted two step screenshots, and produced an xcresult; mandatory visual inspection passed orientation, layout, content, and black-screen checks for both images. The controlled mismatch exited `1` as designed and emitted `reference.png`, `failed.png`, and `diff.png`. Focused contracts, strict Swift formatting, Python/shell syntax, deterministic workspace validation, unsigned macOS host/provider validation, all 455 Swift tests, and `swift build` passed.
 - OWNERSHIP SPLIT: The build host proves unsigned native macOS `build-for-testing` only and reports runtime as explicitly deferred to `TASK-260822-3q4grm`; that task owns signed fixture-host/XCUITest runtime proof on the dedicated test Mac. No provider/system extension is built by either UI-test scheme; no app/provider installation, native Mac fixture launch, VPN preference, tunnel, route, interface, packet-filter, or DNS operation runs here.
 - VALIDATION ANOMALY: A post-rework full `swift test` run exited `1` because the unrelated libssh2 `clientAndServerRekey` M0 gate did not observe `.closed` before its assertion; the run otherwise reached all 455 tests and reported the existing 25 known ReluxNIOSSH issues. An immediate exact `mandatoryGate` rerun passed all 18 argument rows (exit `0`, nine known unavailable-adapter issues), so the failure is retained as a transport-suite timing anomaly rather than attributed to the UI-test infrastructure.
 - REVIEW REWORK: POSIX `set -e` is suppressed inside a function used as an `if` condition, so the first smoke implementation could return a successful Xcode status after a failed screenshot extractor. The runtime row now captures extractor and validator exits explicitly, independently validates the schema/count and both non-empty step-named PNGs, and records separate Xcode, artifact, row, and aggregate exits. A production-script regression injects extractor exit `42` and proves the aggregate exits `1`; the real build-host smoke and all 455 Swift tests pass after the fix.
 
 ### 2350 — SSH profile and credential tests are fake-only and bounded (TASK-260715-3cv3r4)
 - FINDING: The pre-existing macOS credential suite obtained a real system-domain Keychain handle for every fake-client test and created, wrote, queried, and deleted throwaway Keychains in one boundary test. That violated this task's binding fake-only execution boundary even though no production credential was used.
 - FIX: `MacOSSystemKeychainHandle` now has an inert internal fixture identity accepted only by injected fake Security clients; the live client rejects fixture handles before its injectable matcher, and a spy proves zero `SecItemCopyMatching` reachability. The suite no longer calls any live Security API and asserts one exact scoped reference query, no enumeration/fallback, malformed-reference zero calls, cancellation cleanup, passphrase states, and 16 bounded secret-lifecycle repetitions.
 - VERIFICATION: Six focused fake-only Swift suites passed 53 tests. The real coordinator boundary rejects every invalid profile class before injected Keychain/network fakes; all nine `SSHHostKeyDecision` cases traverse the candidate-neutral transport seam with `hostPolicy -> credentialLookup -> authentication` only on accepted paths. One independently owned lifecycle registry retains concrete task, connection, observer, and callback tokens across all 16 bounded iterations; gated cancellation observes all four non-zero, and balanced teardown restores the same registry baseline after success, every rejecting host decision, an injected thrown policy, and cancellation without assigning counters to zero. Three additional cleanup/redaction matrix repetitions passed; captured-log prohibited-data, test-source live-Security, public-fixture, live-network, and self-reset-counter scans returned no matches. Coverage reported 87.75% affected lines and 87.04% affected functions; strict Swift format, core boundaries, and diff checks exited 0. The first focused compile exited 1 on a missing explicit `return`; the corrected rerun and every subsequent gate exited 0. No real Keychain, SSH connection, NetworkExtension runtime, VPN configuration, route, DNS, interface, or packet-filter operation ran.
 
 ### 0035 — M0 binding gate locks the exact retained ReluxNIOSSH tree (TASK-260720-1qhxqa rework 10)
 - REVIEW FINDING: Revision 9 validated the accepted retained ReluxNIOSSH commit, archive, patch, and license metadata but not the checked-in retained source bytes. Narrowing `ReluxPolicies.maximumPayloadBytes` to `1` therefore retained `productionCompositionPermitted=true`.
 - FIX: The immutable binding now pins the deterministic sorted path/file-SHA-256 identity and exact 148-file count of the retained tree, excluding only build caches. The production call site recomputes both and fails with stable `REPOSITORY-SSH-PIN` evidence on any missing, extra, narrowed, or changed retained file.
