     1	# Legacy-to-generated migration isolation
     2	
     3	This repository integrates the generated M1 tunnel runtime without replacing
     4	or migrating the legacy `relux-works/relux-proxy` SwiftPM application. The
     5	accepted M0 preservation baseline is `TASK-260715-14lk3y`; its frozen source is
     6	the signed `v0.1.0` tag at
     7	`2557aba1c030d0643d76e0bc3b185f6d5fd172e1`.
     8	
     9	## Product boundary
    10	
    11	| Surface | Legacy lane — unchanged | Generated M1 lane | Isolation rule |
    12	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
    13	| Repository | `relux-works/relux-proxy` | `relux-works/relux-tunnel` | Separate Git roots; the generated repository does not recreate legacy-owned paths. |
    14	| Package/product | SwiftPM `ReluxProxy` executable | SwiftPM `ReluxTunnel` libraries and `ReluxTunnelHarness`; Tuist `ReluxProxyMac` host | The legacy package imports no `ReluxTunnelCore`, adapter, HEV, or native product. The generated package defines no exact `ReluxProxy` product or target. |
    15	| Tests | `ReluxProxyTests` | Generated host/provider and package test targets | No shared target or test product identity. |
    16	| Application | `dist/ReluxProxy.app` | `ReluxProxyMac.app` | Build roots and executable names are distinct. |
    17	| Provider | None | `works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel.systemextension` | The provider exists only in the generated application bundle. |
    18	| Bundle identifiers | `works.relux.proxy` | Host `works.relux.tunnel.mac`; provider `works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel` | Exact identifiers must remain unequal. |
    19	| Launch behavior | SwiftUI `MenuBarExtra`, macOS 14 | Accessory `NSApplication` host plus NetworkExtension system-extension mode, macOS 15 | Generated launch code neither opens the legacy bundle nor installs a legacy LaunchAgent. The generated host's installer-launcher service remains under its distinct bundle identity. |
    20	| Defaults | Standard bundle domain `works.relux.proxy`; `sshHost=relux`, `sshAccount=administrator`, `localPort=1080` | Standard bundle domain `works.relux.tunnel.mac`; no reuse of the three legacy keys | No implicit defaults import or write-through. |
    21	| Keychain | No v0.1.0 product Keychain namespace | Read-only system-domain service `works.relux.tunnel.credential.v1`; deferred iOS group `$(AppIdentifierPrefix)works.relux.tunnel.shared` | No generated lookup uses the legacy defaults domain or a legacy-owned service. |
    22	| Launch agents | None in the v0.1.0 product/release baseline | None owned by M1 | Runner or updater operations may not substitute a legacy label or path. |
    23	| Release entry points | `make app`, `make dmg`, `scripts/build-app.sh`, `scripts/create-dmg.sh`, legacy release workflow | Credential-free generated build/validation only; no application release path is claimed by M1 | Generated scripts and workflows must not create `ReluxProxy.dmg`, `ReluxProxy-v*`, or `dist/ReluxProxy.app`. |
    24	| Stable artifacts | `ReluxProxy-v<version>-universal.dmg`, `ReluxProxy.dmg` | No generated stable application artifact in M1 | The legacy names remain exclusively owned by the legacy release lane. |
    25	
    26	The complete legacy product-bearing byte inventory remains pinned by
    27	`config/legacy-v0.1.0.sha256` and is verified by
    28	`scripts/check-legacy-preservation.sh`. The complementary
    29	`scripts/check-migration-isolation.py` command verifies the cross-repository
    30	dependency, identity, storage, launch, release, generated-project, and optional
    31	built-product boundary.
    32	
    33	## Automated gates
    34	
    35	Run the source and release boundary plus its adversarial checks against a
    36	detached v0.1.0 checkout:
    37	
    38	```sh
    39	make check-migration-isolation LEGACY_ROOT=/path/to/legacy-v0.1.0
    40	make test-migration-isolation LEGACY_ROOT=/path/to/legacy-v0.1.0
    41	```
    42	
    43	`scripts/validate-credential-free.sh` is the production integration call site.
    44	It runs the accepted legacy preservation guard, the migration-isolation CLI,
    45	and the negative suite after generated host/provider validation. The negative
    46	suite drives that same CLI and narrows the boundary with generated and legacy
    47	cross-links, bundle/defaults/Keychain collisions, built-product collisions,
    48	and release-script substitution. Each mutation must be refused for its named
    49	reason.
    50	
    51	When `--generated-project` and `--products-root` are supplied, the gate also
    52	checks the generated PBX target/product inventory and both Debug and Release
    53	host/provider bundles. An exact legacy target, app, executable, or DMG name in
    54	those products is a failure.
    55	
    56	## Deferred ownership
    57	
    58	This task does not migrate users or data, delete legacy code, change either
    59	release path, reconcile UI, ship both products, or decide retirement timing.
    60	
    61	- M4 `TASK-260715-35nc5m` owns the coexistence, replacement, or retirement
    62	  decision and any user-facing/import behavior.
    63	- M5 `TASK-260715-1tzaed` owns the macOS release identity, entitlement, and data
    64	  migration contract after the M4 decision.
    65	
    66	Until both decisions are accepted, the only valid behavior is independent
    67	coexistence with zero implicit migration.
